# Line endings are part of these files' contents, not a local preference.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is set system-wide on many Windows machines, which
# rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. That silently changes bytes on disk while
# `git status` still reports a clean tree, and it breaks anything that hashes
# or byte-matches a checked-in file:
#   - mocks/ golden streams are replayed byte-for-byte and their sha256 is
#     pinned in scripts/readable-fixture-classification.json
#   - CSS/TS sources are matched by tests that write multi-line selectors and
#     snippets with \n
# Normalising the whole tree to LF keeps the working copy identical to the
# commit on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.node binary
*.sqlite binary

# Windows-only scripts stay CRLF so PowerShell and cmd read them correctly.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

design-systems/*/design-tokens.json text eol=lf
design-systems/*/tailwind-v4.css text eol=lf
